---
description: Conventions for the SpaceX React take-home assignment
alwaysApply: true
---

- Build the application using React and TypeScript.
- Prefer functional components and React hooks.
- Use descriptive variable and function names.
- Keep API logic, cache logic, UI components, and styling separate.
- Avoid unnecessary libraries, abstractions, and premature optimization.
- Make loading, error, empty, and cached-data states explicit.
- Ensure filters reset pagination and prevent stale results from appearing.
- Implement accessible controls, keyboard navigation, and visible focus states.
- Use semantic HTML and responsive CSS.
- Avoid adding useMemo, useCallback, or memo everywhere; optimize when justified.
- Test edge cases before considering a feature complete.
- Run the available tests and production build after meaningful changes.
- Do not silently omit assignment requirements.
- Explain architectural decisions and non-obvious tradeoffs.
